# Frontend Rules (React)

- Keep page-level state orchestration in `src/App.jsx`; avoid duplicating global state elsewhere.
- Put feature-specific logic inside `src/features/<feature>/`.
- Reuse shared components from `src/features/shared/` before creating new primitives.
- Maintain current visual language: compact cards, clear labels, practical actions.
- Keep text concise and school-admin friendly (non-technical phrasing).
- For dashboard/report insights, show action-oriented guidance (what to do next).
- Avoid large monolithic components; extract helpers for transformations/insights.
- Preserve existing navigation and page IDs used by `navigate(...)`.
- For timetable diagnostics/shortage insights, show class context (standard + division + subject) instead of subject-only summaries.
- **Generated timetable UI:** resolve **`report.unscheduled`** and grid columns against **`timetable.sourceState`** when present (`pickTimetableSnapshotLists`, `periodGridForTimetableView` in `TimetablePages.jsx`; **`findEntityById`** in `src/features/shared/idLookups.js` for string/number id parity). Pass snapshot **`periodSlots`** / **`workingDays`** into **`TimetableGrid`** so Break/Lunch headers align with **`entries`** slot numbers; Dashboard completion bullets use the same snapshot lists.
- **Manual edit mode (division view):** swap/move/add via `manualEditActions.js` + API helpers; show repair steps from `valid-add-options` when add is blocked; apply `withLiveTimetableReport` after client-side undo/optimistic updates so score/unscheduled match `entries`. Teacher view stays read-only.
- **Placement preferences UI:** `PillMultiSelect` for subjects and divisions in `SchedulingPages.jsx`; saving applies the same rule to all selected subjects/divisions—keep exclude vs fixed-placement guards consistent.
- Prefer actionable quick links from diagnostics cards (`navigate("teachers"|"subjects"|"rules"|"periods")`) when recommending fixes.
- Keep sidebar release footer format as `V<version> (<build-number>)`; show `LOCAL · DEV` tags only in local dev mode.

## UI Change Checklist

- Works on mobile and desktop breakpoints.
- No overflow/regression in cards, tables, or action bars; give modal footers (e.g. multi-step **Subjects** wizard) clear separation from scrollable content and enough bottom padding/safe-area for primary actions.
- Existing flows still work: generate timetable, view timetable, exports, settings.

